Package: fuxi-modem
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: fuxi port <noreply@localhost>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: fuxi-device, modemmanager (>= 1.25.95), libmm-glib0 (>= 1.25.95), 81voltd (>= 1.2.0), libqmi-proxy, libqmi-utils, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-qmi-1.0, gir1.2-qrtr-1.0, qrtr-tools, network-manager, util-linux, iproute2, polkitd, pkexec
Recommends: gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1
Description: Xiaomi 13 (fuxi, SM8550) cellular glue for mainline Linux
 Dual-SIM modem support on top of ModemManager / 81voltd / libqmi:
  - patched ModemManager (SIM slot / subscription binding, fuxi LOC GPS_RAW) and
    81voltd-sub2 (IMS/VoLTE on SIM 2), installed under /usr/libexec/fuxi and
    switched in with systemd drop-ins
  - fuxi-qmi-proxy (resident qmi-proxy), fuxi-uim-provision (UIM sessions
    before ModemManager), fuxi-modem-keeper, SIM 2 SMS/call listener and IMS
    heal, optional SIM 2 data card
  - fuxi-simctl + "SIM settings" app (polkit-authorised SIM switching)
  - fuxi-gnss-session: bounded on-demand LOC sessions with aggregate output
